mode: "100644"
text: "# Promise template, design checklist, A/B plan + two worked examples\n\n## The promise sentence (write this first)\n```\nThis video shows [audience] how/why [specific outcome or problem] by revealing [specific mechanism].\n-> Thumbnail SHOWS the hook visually; Title TELLS the context. They never repeat.\n```\n\n## Design checklist (evaluate before handing off the brief)\n```\n[ ] One clear focal point (1-2 hero elements); minimal/blurred background\n[ ] Face: genuine expression + gaze toward the key element (or no face if it adds nothing)\n[ ] Contrast: complementary pair, avoid YouTube red/white, 60-30-10, passes the B&W test, OK in light + dark\n[ ] Text: 0-4 bold sans-serif words + outline, ~20-30% of frame, does NOT duplicate the title\n[ ] Mobile: legible at ~168x94 px; competitor-preview for the target keyword\n[ ] Safe zones: nothing critical in the bottom-right (duration badge) or bottom 15% / corners\n[ ] Brand: consistent font/palette/layout with the channel's other thumbnails\n```\n\n## Spec block\n```\nSize 1280x720, 16:9, JPG or PNG. Cap is 50MB since early 2026 (was 2MB; the extra headroom is for 4K/TV). RGB.\nCreated in an image/design tool (nano-banana / ideogram / Canva / a designer) -- NOT by WoopSocial.\nYouTube custom thumbnail: uploaded NATIVELY in YouTube Studio (WoopSocial has no thumbnail field).\nTikTok / IG-Reel COVER: different -- a frame/card set via WoopSocial's `cover` field (tiktok-video-publishing / IG skill).\n```\n\n## A/B test plan template (native Test & Compare)\n```\nVariant A: [promise/emotion 1]   e.g. surprised face + \"$0 to $10K\"\nVariant B: [promise/emotion 2]   e.g. object-only product hero, no text\nVariant C: [promise/emotion 3]   e.g. before/after split\nRule: change ONE meaningful variable across the set; each tests a different reason to click.\nWinner: YouTube picks by WATCH-TIME SHARE (not CTR), up to ~14 days. Not for Shorts. Needs Advanced\nFeatures + traffic (<1k impressions/week -> inconclusive). Test & Compare can also test TITLES or\ntitle+thumbnail combos (since Dec 2025) -- test the packaging as the unit it is.\nA HUMAN uploads + runs it in Studio. Log the result for next time.\n```\n\n## Worked example 1 — tutorial, established face (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nPROMISE: shows freelancers how to run their business in Notion in 20 min. TITLE tells \"Notion for Freelancers (2026)\".\nTHUMB shows: my genuine \"wait, that's it?\" face (gaze -> the dashboard), one clean dashboard hero, dark bg,\nyellow accent, text \"20 MIN SETUP\" (not repeating the title). Mobile-checked at 168x94. Brief -> image tool; I upload + Test&Compare 3 emotions.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — faceless, abstract topic (warm studio voice)\n```\nPROMISE: shows small studios why their cash flow stalls. No face (concept-focused) -> the hero is a simple\nred-line-going-flat chart on a deep navy background, one arrow pointing at the dip. No text, or just \"THE GAP\".\nHigh contrast, passes the B&W test, reads on a phone. Raster by the design tool; uploaded natively; best-practice + preview (low traffic, A/B may be inconclusive).\n```\n\nBoth: promise written first; thumbnail+title as a unit; one focal point; honest emotion; high contrast +\nshort/no text; mobile-legible + safe zones; raster made by an image tool/designer; YouTube thumbnail\nuploaded + tested natively; CTR from native analytics (never fabricated).\n"
